    "message": "fix(release): list the archive to a file, not into grep -q\n\nThe stamp guard I just added was itself a race. This step runs under\n`pipefail`, and `grep -q` exits at the first match, so the lister gets\nSIGPIPE and the pipeline reports *its* failure — which `!` then reads as\n\"stamp missing\" and fails the release.\n\nCaught by a dispatch dry-run: linux-arm64 failed with `tar: stdout: write\nerror` while linux-amd64, darwin-arm64 and windows-amd64 all passed. The\narchiver usually finishes writing before grep exits and sometimes does\nnot, so it would have failed real releases at random.\n\nReproduced locally with a 4,000-entry listing: the piped form raises a\nfalse alarm every time, listing to a file passes, and it still catches an\narchive with the stamp genuinely stripped.\n\nThe Windows leg of that same run is the useful result: 7z does carry a\ndot-named file into the zip, which was the one assumption behind stamping\nthat could not be checked from a PR dry-run.",
